.git
*.log

# --- 2026-08-31 CVE sweep: keep dev/CI-only artifacts OUT of the build context ---
# `COPY . .` in the build stage swept these into the shipped image, where a scanner
# then found their (irrelevant-at-runtime) CVEs and their bytes were pure attack surface.
#
# .claude — Claude Code's working dir. It holds LINKED GIT WORKTREES of other sessions
# (.claude/worktrees/*), so `COPY . .` was dragging ~190 MiB of a second, third, … full
# checkout — each carrying its own committed tools/openapi/bin/oasdiff Go binary — into
# the image. Never needed by the build or at runtime.
.claude
# CI workflow definitions — never part of the runtime image.
.github
#
# NOT excluded here, deliberately: `tools/openapi/bin/oasdiff-linux-amd64`. The oasdiff Go binary
# is a BUILD/CI tool (the /v1 breaking-change gate), never read at runtime — but `.dockerignore`
# applies to EVERY build that uses the repo root as context, and `tools/ci-image/Dockerfile`
# legitimately `COPY`s oasdiff into the CI toolchain image. Excluding it here broke that build
# (`COPY tools/openapi/bin/... not found`). So the scpd RUNTIME image drops oasdiff in its own
# build stage instead (see Dockerfile) — keeping its CVEs out of the shipped server without
# starving the CI image build.
